# Round enqthread: the V4.1 prompt batch's shadow copies the block's q8_1 planes only where the tile
# path reads them (chain/ffn/batch.rs FfnBatch::reads_planes: a gate's catcher alone), so on the
# default grouped GEMM a full chunk of a fused card layer issues 2 entries fewer. Bits and kernels
# are unchanged (the planes' one reader is the tile block); the entry count moves with the flow
# model (tools/flow/ds41_prefill.py CP1 / CP2, prefill.rs shadow_entries). The round derives; the
# lead times the sitting.
#
# Decomposition [derived, A6000, place a, 1017 Q3_K_M, P = 4096, from the lead's 2026-11-15 sitting's
# 320 `stat prefill lb` records]: the cut is 26,344 entries a call by the records' chunk counts
# (26,600 by the flow model at --place gate), ~120 a block layer-batch, entries_shadow 493.8 ->
# ~374 a layer-batch. The host issues an entry in t_e ~2.4..3.0 us and blocks while the stream's
# launch queue holds 1,021 entries the card has not started (this round's probe: 1,021 at the
# driver's default, 2,045 at CUDA_SCALE_LAUNCH_QUEUES=2x, 4,093 at 4x, every entry kind one slot,
# driver 615.71.09). A host/card replay of the records with those two terms gives chain 8,240..8,243
# ms against 8,233 measured and enqueue 1,530..1,543 against 1,538.5: the enqueue_lb 7.0 is ~3.1 ms
# of issue and ~2.5 ms of back-pressure, not launch CPU alone. The cut removes ~64..76 ms of issue
# and ~40..66 ms of card time (2 dtod 2.35 us + 2 x 0.90 us gap a chunk); with the queue still full
# half of it returns as route waits: chain -0.5..-0.8 % (41..66 ms of a ~8.55 s prompt call).
# Resource timeline per layer-batch: host thread enqueue 7.0 + union 30.2 (the wall, a sum); card
# ~33..34 under it; the queue's back-pressure ties the host to the card's progress. The flow levers
# (a second enqueue thread, a deeper launch queue) are priced in the round's report and the sibling
# card enqthread-lq2.card; this card prices the cut alone.
kind: ab
question: does dropping the shadow's plane copies off the GEMM path shorten the V4.1 prompt call by
  their issue and card time?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 4096, prose, depth 0, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 Q3_K_M, --place a, the default
  levers (group 2, residency and host streaming on), RTX A6000 - (this tree - base) / base, paired
  by round
unit: %
predict: +0.4..+0.8
rounds: 8
sd: 0.25 % the lead's 2026-11-15 cardexp sitting (A6000, place a, prose P = 4096, 3f018b518 against 4e28e0a54), the pp ratio's per-round SD 0.35 % over 8 rounds over sqrt 2 for one run
condition: this tree's generate_ds41 and 78564829d's (main before the change: /root/repo/bloomery's build, code-equal to 7bfa7c476
  before the lease, a bin: arm) alternate in one lease, BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=8 just depth-gpu-ds41
  prose:4096@BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 bin:/root/repo/bloomery/target/release/generate_ds41:prose:4096@BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1,
  the order rotated every round; both arms' plan prints name the same residency word and
  card_experts; in every round the stat lines read: this tree's entries_shadow 370..378 a
  layer-batch against the base's 493.8 and entries_route equal across arms (counts: a binary that
  does not show them is not the tree's), union_lb and card_out_lb within 0.5 ms of the base's,
  card_in_lb 0.1..0.35 ms under it, enqueue_lb 0.4..0.9 ms under the base's 7.0, wait_lb at most
  1.0; no row carries [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]
decide-in: land the cut; then time enqthread-lq2.card (the launch queue at 2x, same binary), the
  larger term the replay names
decide-below: read the arms' stat lines: if entries_shadow fell as predicted but enqueue_lb fell less
  than 0.4 ms a layer-batch, the issue cost is not a per-entry term: the launch queue's back-pressure
  holds the host, so time enqthread-lq2.card next and leave the cut to land with it
decide-above: the plane copies cost the card more than 2.35 us a chunk (card_in_lb fell more than
  0.35 ms): re-measure the shadow chunk's D2D term in the flow model's constants before the next cut
